# Testing

- Every behavior change gets a test in the owning service (`tests/`)
- FastAPI: prefer `TestClient` / `httpx` against the app; assert status + response shape
- Domain logic: unit-test pure functions without network or real LLM calls
- Google ADK: mock model/runner in unit tests; don’t call live Gemini in CI
- DB: prefer migration apply on clean Postgres in integration jobs; keep unit tests DB-free unless using a test container
- No flaky sleeps or realtime dependencies in unit tests

```python
# ✅ GOOD — contract smoke test
def test_health() -> None:
    assert client.get("/health").json()["status"] == "ok"

# ❌ BAD — live LLM in unit test
def test_agent():
    assert call_gemini("hi")  # network + cost + flake
```

Run: `cd <service> && uv run pytest`
